<title>USA: Affinity Entertainment gets loan-BARRON'S.</title>
<headline>Affinity Entertainment gets loan-BARRON'S.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Affinity Entertainment has an agreement for an unnamed &quot;major European entity&quot; to loan the company $48.4 million at nine percent interest over five years, according to a report in Barron's.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the agreement gives the lender the right to convert 20 percent of the loan into Affinity shares at a minimum price of 10.</p>
<p>Affinity stock closed Friday at 2-31/32.</p>
<p>Last week, Affinity said that its equity private placement with Baron Banker Ltd was terminated and the four million shares of common stock purchased by Baron were cancelled.</p>
</text>
